## Summary

I enforced the architectural boundary by introducing a `legacy_core` compatibility shim in the `codex-tui` crate.

**1. Added the `legacy_core` module** in `codex-rs/tui/src/lib.rs` (accessible as `crate::legacy_core` from anywhere in the library crate since it's `pub(crate)`):

```rust
pub(crate) mod legacy_core {
    pub use codex_core::config;
    pub use codex_core::config_loader;
    pub use codex_core::plugins;
    pub use codex_core::skills;
    // Only referenced from `#[cfg(test)]` code within this crate.
    #[allow(unused_imports)]
    pub use codex_core::test_support;
}
```

I re-exported the whole modules rather than enumerating items — this satisfies the "at minimum" list (`Config`, `ConfigBuilder`, `Constrained`, `ConstraintError`; the six `config_loader` types; `OPENAI_CURATED_MARKETPLACE_NAME`, `PluginCapabilitySummary`; `skills::model::SkillMetadata`; `construct_model_info_offline`, `all_model_presets`, `get_model_offline`) and also covers every other `codex_core::{config,config_loader,plugins,skills,test_support}::…` path the TUI already uses, so nothing breaks.

**2. Rewrote all usages** across 28 source files under `codex-rs/tui/src` (including inline `#[cfg(test)]` modules), replacing `codex_core::{config,config_loader,plugins,skills,test_support}::…` with `crate::legacy_core::…`.

**Notable decisions:**
- `src/main.rs` is a *separate binary crate*, where `crate::` refers to the binary root (which has no `legacy_core`) and the `pub(crate)` shim isn't visible. I left its one usage on the direct `codex_core::config_loader::LoaderOverrides` path.
- I did not touch the top-level `codex-rs/tui/tests/` directory, per the constraint. Those integration tests still reference `codex_core` directly and continue to compile.
- The `test_support` re-export gets a scoped `#[allow(unused_imports)]` since it's only consumed from `#[cfg(test)]` code (otherwise unused in release builds).

